// python/annotation-code: the code inside string annotations, for the rules that check it as Ruff does.
//
// Interface
//   ann_tree_node(n)   n is a node of the parsed tree of a string Ruff reads as a type (F601, F632)
//
// Ruff parses each string type definition (`x: "List[int]"`, `cast("T", v)`, `TypeVar("T", bound="B")`, nested
// ones too) and runs its rules over the tree, so the code in it is checked like any other. The engine makes a
// string's tree only for a rule that asks for it (`parsed`, core), and a string Ruff cannot parse has none, so
// nothing is checked in it (Ruff reports F722 there instead).
//   variable: "123 is not y"           F632 at the comparison inside the string
//   j: "'%(a)s' % {'a': 1, 'a': 2}"    F601 at the second 'a'
#include "core.rerail"

.decl ann_tree_node(n: node)
ann_tree_node(n) :- string_annotation(s), parsed(s, "annotation", r), (n = r ; within(n, r)).
